[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:48. The Silent Village]
[00:00.541] Passage 48. | 第48篇课文
[00:02.195] The Silent Village. | 寂静的村庄
[00:05.105] In this much-traveled world, there are still thousands of places which are inaccessible to tourists. | 在这个人们常常出行旅游的世界上，仍然有成千上万个游客无法到达的地方。
[00:12.435] We always assume that villagers in remote places are friendly and hospitable. | 我们总是认为，偏远地区的村民是友善好客的。
[00:18.030] But people who are cut off not only from foreign tourists, | 但是，那些不仅与外国游客隔绝，
[00:21.770] but even from their own countrymen, | 甚至与本国同胞也隔绝的人，
[00:23.935] can be hostile to travelers. | 可能对旅行者怀有敌意。
[00:26.350] Visits to really remote villages are seldom enjoyable. | 探访那些真正偏远的村庄，很少是愉快的经历。
[00:30.095] As my wife and I discovered during a tour through the Balkans. | 正如我和妻子在巴尔干地区旅行时所发现的。
[00:34.630] We had spent several days in a small town, | 我们在一个小镇上度过了几天，
[00:38.285] and visited a number of old churches in the vicinity. | 参观了附近一些古老的教堂。
[00:41.730] These attracted many visitors, | 这些教堂吸引了许多游客，
[00:44.195] for they were not only of great architectural interest, | 因为它们不仅具有巨大的建筑价值，
[00:47.055] but contained a large number of beautifully preserved frescoes as well. | 而且还保存着大量精美的壁画。
[00:51.895] On the day before our departure, | 在我们出发的前一天，
[00:54.830] several busloads of tourists descended on the town. | 几辆满载游客的巴士抵达了小镇。
[00:58.820] This was more than we could bear, | 这超出了我们的承受范围，
[01:00.840] so we decided to spend our last day exploring the countryside. | 所以我们决定最后一天去乡下探险。
[01:05.435] Taking a path which led out of the town, | 沿着一条通出小镇的小路，
[01:08.615] we crossed a few fields, | 我们穿过了几片田野，
[01:10.590] until we came to a dense wood. | 直到我们来到一片茂密的树林。
[01:13.125] We expected the path to end abruptly. | 我们以为这条小路会突然中断。
[01:16.655] But we found that it traced its way through the trees. | 但我们发现它蜿蜒穿行于树林之中。
[01:20.590] We tramped through the wood for over two hours, | 我们在树林里跋涉了两个多小时，
[01:24.340] until we arrived at a deep stream. | 直到我们来到一条很深的溪流边。
[01:27.430] We could see that the path continued on the other side, | 我们看到小路在对岸继续延伸，
[01:30.950] but we had no idea how we could get across the stream. | 但我们不知道如何才能过河。
[01:34.230] Suddenly my wife spotted a boat, | 突然，我妻子发现了一艘船，
[01:36.425] moored to the bank. | 停泊在岸边。
[01:38.015] In it there was a boatman, | 船上有一个船夫，
[01:39.840] fast asleep. | 睡得很香。
[01:41.270] We gently woke him up, | 我们轻轻地叫醒了他，
[01:43.435] and asked him to ferry us to the other side. | 请他把我们摆渡到对岸。
[01:46.405] Though he was reluctant to do so at first, | 虽然他一开始不情愿，
[01:49.095] we eventually persuaded him to take us. | 但我们最终说服了他带我们过去。
[01:52.655] The path led to a tiny village, | 这条小路通向一个很小的村庄，
[01:56.290] perched on the steep sides of a mountain. | 坐落在陡峭的山坡上。
[01:59.725] The place consisted of a straggling unmade road | 这个地方由一条蜿蜒崎岖的未铺路组成，
[02:03.474] which was lined on either side by small houses. | 两旁是小房子。
[02:06.240] Even under a clear blue sky, | 即使在晴朗的蓝天下，
[02:08.895] the village looked forbidding, | 村庄也显得令人生畏，
[02:10.745] as all the houses were built of gray mud bricks. | 因为所有的房子都是用灰色的泥砖建造的。
[02:14.725] The village seemed deserted, | 村庄似乎空无一人，
[02:16.900] the only sign of life being an ugly-looking black goat, | 唯一的生命迹象是一只看起来很丑的黑山羊，
[02:20.440] tied to a tree on a short length of rope | 被一根短绳子绑在一棵树上，
[02:22.712] in a field nearby. | 就在附近的一块田地里。
[02:24.485] Sitting down on a dilapidated wooden fence near the field, | 我们坐在田边一处破旧的木栅栏上，
[02:28.275] we opened a couple of tins of sardines, | 打开了两罐沙丁鱼，
[02:30.730] and had a picnic lunch. | 然后吃了野餐。
[02:32.830] All at once I noticed that my wife | 突然，我注意到妻子
[02:35.440] seemed to be filled with alarm. | 似乎充满了警觉。
[02:37.830] Looking up, I saw that we were surrounded by children in rags, | 抬头一看，我看到我们被一群衣衫褴褛的孩子包围着，
[02:41.970] who were looking at us silently as we ate. | 他们在我们吃饭时默默地看着我们。
[02:45.065] We offered them food, | 我们给了他们食物，
[02:47.130] and spoke to them kindly. | 并亲切地与他们交谈。
[02:49.430] But they remained motionless. | 但他们仍然一动不动。
[02:52.095] I concluded that they were simply | 我断定他们只是
[02:54.555] shy of strangers. | 害羞，不愿与陌生人接触。
[02:56.410] When we later walked down the main street of the village, | 当我们后来沿着村子的主街走下去时，
[02:59.325] we were followed by a silent procession of children. | 一群孩子默默地跟在我们后面。
[03:03.045] The village, which had seemed deserted, | 这个原本看起来空无一人的村庄，
[03:05.665] immediately came to life. | 立刻变得热闹起来。
[03:07.640] Faces appeared at windows. | 窗户里出现了面孔。
[03:10.105] Men in shirt-sleeves stood outside their houses | 穿着衬衫的男人站在屋外，
[03:12.959] and glared at us. | 怒视着我们。
[03:14.610] Old women in black shawls | 披着黑色披肩的老妇人
[03:17.095] peered at us from doorways. | 从门道里窥视着我们。
[03:19.560] The most frightening thing of all | 最令人恐惧的是，
[03:22.145] was that not a sound could be heard. | 听不到任何声音。
[03:25.095] There was no doubt that we were | 毫无疑问，我们是
[03:27.215] unwelcome visitors. | 不受欢迎的客人。
[03:29.145] We needed no further warning. | 我们不需要更多的警告。
[03:31.680] Turning back down the main street, | 沿着主街走回去，
[03:33.940] we quickened our pace | 我们加快了脚步，
[03:35.510] and made our way rapidly towards the stream, | 迅速地向溪流走去，
[03:38.495] where we hoped the boatman was waiting. | 我们希望船夫在那里等着。